{
  "case_id": "2020-19-930",
  "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:31 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CIC Services",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CIC Services wants to challenge an IRS notice under the APA. That guidance document subjects an entire industry to a burdensome reporting regime, but it never went through notice-and-comment rulemaking."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CIC Services",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "not the assessment or collection of any tax."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think I heard you say that you're asking that the notice be set aside. But maybe it's a technical matter, but that's not actually what you're asking. You're asking for an injunction against the enforcement of the notice. Does that make a difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Norris. I'd like to get your response or thoughts on Judge Sutton's concurrence in the denial of rehearing en banc, and he expressed one concern that, given the fact that the Anti-Injunction Act and Tax Injunction Act are so often interpreted in parallel, that by vindicating a taxpayer -- federal taxpayer's interests today, we might slight state sovereign concerns tomorrow, creating the risk that too much haste in stopping one abuse of power might open the door to another."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But isn't -- isn't that, as Justice Sotomayor pointed out, just a pleading exercise of how you frame it in your complaint? I'm challenging actually the regulatory part of the regulatory tax, as opposed to the enforcement of the liability itself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Notice 16-66 labels my client's industry a reportable transaction, a kind of scarlet letter that triggers burdensome reporting requirements and makes it much harder to attract clients."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the determination to channel that dispute to refund suits. It's not eliminating review. It's simply channeling it to a different forum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I'm not saying it's not a tax. I'm simply asking how do they get judicial review without paying the tax --the penalty, which I'll call a tax, how do they get judicial review of the lawfulness of the order that says -- or the report that says give us the information? How do they do it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The code says that willfully failing to comply with the reporting requirement is a crime. So I really don't see how they can get review without committing a crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bond",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOND: So I think -- well, I would put it a little bit differently. I'd say that there is a bright-line rule that covers cases where the complaint on its face seeks relief that would restrain a tax. That's this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cameron T. Norris",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF CAMERON T. NORRIS ON BEHALF OF PETITIONER\n\nMR. NORRIS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. It's not every day that the United States Government asks citizens to deliberately violate the tax code, but that's my friend's position in this case, and that's a critical distinction for purposes of reaching the right decision here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-930",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ee6bc7a84652d28057534b3637f2328cde2c021f434ba7b7378bd956fa13de1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee6bc7a8465-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
